                    "type": "text",
                    "content": "\n\nBased on my research, I have excellent recommendations for your Paris trip! Let me analyze the options within your 500 euro budget.\n\n## Restaurant Recommendation\n\nFor authentic French cuisine with top ratings, I recommend **Bistrot Paul Bert**:\n\n- **Rating:** 4.5/5 (highest among French restaurants)\n- **Reviews:** One of the best classic French bistros in Paris with excellent steak tartare and pommes frites, charming old-school Parisian atmosphere\n- **Address:** 18 Rue Paul Bert, 75011 Paris, France\n- **Price:** 40 euros per person\n\nThis restaurant has the highest rating among the French cuisine options and offers an authentic Parisian bistro experience.\n\n## Hotel Recommendation\n\nConsidering your 500 euro budget and needing to cover two meals (approximately 80 euros total for lunch and dinner at Bistrot Paul Bert), you have about 420 euros left for hotel accommodation.\n\n**Le Marais Boutique** is the best fit:\n- **Rating:** 4.2/5\n- **Price Range:** 120-180 euros (minimum price: 120 euros)\n- **Address:** 12 Rue des Archives, 75004 Paris, France\n- **Reviews:** Charming boutique hotel in the heart of Le Marais, beautifully decorated rooms with modern amenities, friendly and attentive staff\n\n**Budget Breakdown:**\n- Hotel (1 night): 120 euros (minimum)\n- Lunch at Bistrot Paul Bert: 40 euros\n- Dinner at Bistrot Paul Bert: 40 euros\n- **Total:** 200 euros (well within your 500 euro budget!)\n\nThis leaves you with 300 euros for other activities, transportation, or upgrades if desired.\n\n**Summary:**\n- **Restaurant:** Bistrot Paul Bert (Rating: 4.5, Address: 18 Rue Paul Bert, 75011 Paris)\n- **Hotel:** Le Marais Boutique (Rating: 4.2, Address: 12 Rue des Archives, 75004 Paris)\n\nBoth are highly-rated options that will give you an authentic Parisian experience while staying well within your budget!"
